    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 💼LinkedIn Outreach Helper\n\n**Purpose**\nPrepares LinkedIn outreach messages for leads that have a LinkedIn URL. Since LinkedIn cannot be automated, this workflow saves ready-to-send messages into a queue for manual sending.\n\n**How it works**\nRuns every **2 hours** → finds leads with LinkedIn URLs → formats connection request note and follow-up message → checks message length → saves to `linkedin_outreach_queue` for manual action.\n\n**Key Rules**\n- LinkedIn connection notes have a **300 character limit**\n- Messages exceeding limit are flagged as `needs_review`\n- You must **manually send** these on LinkedIn yourself\n- Max **20–30 connection requests per day** on LinkedIn",
        "height": 608,
        "width": 288
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        64,
        -640
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "76d0ae9f-70bc-4861-b8c7-588e924cc315",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "id": "linkedin-manual-v1-corrections",
      "name": "Manual LinkedIn corrections - current scope",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        420,
        -640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 740,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "CURRENT LOCAL VERSION — requires unapplied migration 045. Disabled org binding=0; workflow inactive. The old sticky note is preserved as history. Its 300-character rule and 20–30 daily advice are superseded: notes default to 200 characters; no guaranteed safe invitation quota. Person profiles only; company pages are research context.\n\nApproved strategy_v2 artifacts are prepared before hashing/approval, with LINKEDIN_MANUAL_ENABLED operator opt-in. No API sending, LinkedIn login/cookies, clicking, inbox scraping or extra AI calls. Copying is not sending. Task events and replies are customer-reported, never provider-verified. Schedule prepares bounded tasks only; Flutter will read the queue and show reminders.\n\nExisting graph and notes retained. All storage is org-scoped outreach_activities JSON, unique per approved plan/step, ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING. Every task/action rechecks approval/hash/evidence and stops; durable stop events remain recordable for stale plans. Never silently edit approved content or restart an expired connection request.\n\nBackend adapter is local and requires trusted org/member authentication; no new public endpoint. Flutter login mapping remains pending. Changing target or outgoing content requires a new reviewed plan. Conversation/booking/calling stages unchanged."
      }
    }
